{"name":"Dreamcatcher","hex":"#a5b2a9","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dreamcatcher","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A decorative Native American object in the form of a hoop and net with attachments such as feathers, traditionally believed by the Ojibwa to “filter out” bad dreams."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dreamcatcher"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dreamcatcher","blocks":[{"text":"In some Native American and First Nations cultures, a dreamcatcher is a handmade willow hoop, on which is woven a net or web. It may also be decorated with sacred items such as certain feathers or beads. Traditionally, dreamcatchers are hung over a cradle or bed as protection. It originates in Anishinaabe culture as \"the spider web charm\" – asubakacin 'net-like' ; bwaajige ngwaagan 'dream snare' – a hoop with woven string or sinew meant to replicate a spider's web, used as a protective charm for infants."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Dreamcatcher_-_Royal_Ontario_Museum_%2840194857691%29.jpg/330px-Dreamcatcher_-_Royal_Ontario_Museum_%2840194857691%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dreamcatcher","wikidata":"Q257179"},{"title":"Dreamcatcher (group)","blocks":[{"text":"Dreamcatcher is a South Korean girl group formed by Dreamcatcher Company. The group consists of seven members: JiU, SuA, Siyeon, Handong, Yoohyeon, Dami, and Gahyun. They made their official debut on January 13, 2017, with the single album Nightmare."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/190426_%EB%93%9C%EB%A6%BC%EC%BA%90%EC%B3%90_%EC%86%A1%EB%8F%84_%EB%B6%88%EA%BD%83%EC%B6%95%EC%A0%9C.jpg/330px-190426_%EB%93%9C%EB%A6%BC%EC%BA%90%EC%B3%90_%EC%86%A1%EB%8F%84_%EB%B6%88%EA%BD%83%EC%B6%95%EC%A0%9C.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dreamcatcher_(group)",